I imagine that the only way the game can deal with items on the same 
square is either to make them separate items (that is, unattached, so 
that any of them can be picked up without disturbing the others) or make 
one a container which houses the rest (how statues actually are handled). 
While it may not make sense that you cannot *see* Perseus's shield, it 
does make sense that you could not *get* it without breaking the statue 
(at least the hand/arm holding the shield).

Do wands of probing reveal the contents of containers? They should. Also, 
arguably, blessed stethoscopes. 

